{"design_rationale": "Observed positive gain with 1-2s lag and self-drain to near-zero. Key nonlinearity: u=0.4 holds ~0.19 while u=0.5 holds ~0.588, then shallow slope 0.55->0.65 (+0.01y per +0.05u, local pump-rate gain ~0.08-0.10/s per unit u). Hold for 0.6 is ~0.55-0.63, so use conservative feedforward ~0.57 for 0.6 with shallow target dependence and let integral correct residual. PI with Kp=1.0, Ki=0.20 (Ti=5s) gives loop gain ~0.75 with ~2.5s total delay (plant lag + 0.8s EMA filter), stable without D. EMA tau 0.8s suppresses ~0.01 noise without adding lag. Conditional integration (|e|<0.25 and not saturated) plus I clamp [-0.20,0.25] prevents windup from the high-gain 0.4-0.5 region. Far-below error gives P~0.4-0.5 so u saturates at 0.80 for fast fill (~0.028/s, 0.2->0.6 in ~15-20s within 30s settling); near target P shrinks for soft landing. High-y guards (yf>0.80 ->0, yf>0.70 cap 0.25) guarantee no 0.9 cutoff.", "machine_card": "Water reservoir: +u raises y (positive gain). Speed: net rise ~0.022/s at u=0.6 low-y, ~0.029/s at u=0.8 mid-y, ~0.026/s at u=0.8 y~0.5; worst-case bound 0.08/s per unit u. Fill 0.2->0.6 needs ~15-20s at u=0.8. Lag/delay ~1-2s after every step (E3/E4/E5). Dead-zone: none above 0.4, but highly nonlinear: u=0.4 holds ~0.18-0.20 (E1), u=0.5 holds ~0.588 (E7), u=0.55 holds ~0.583 (E8), u=0.6 drifts 0.585->0.60 (E9), u=0.65 drives 0.592->0.619 in 3s (E10); incremental gain ~4.0/unit in 0.4-0.5, ~0.2-0.8/unit near target. Self-draining: u=0 decays 0.395->0.02 in ~19.6s (E3), rate ~0.030/s at y~0.33, ~0.020/s at y~0.13, ~0.014/s at y~0.06, tau ~7-15s. Noise std <0.01 typically (<0.02 max) vs 0.10 band, averaging works.", "operator_note": "Targets 0.6. Starts with pump ~0.8 when far below, eases to ~0.57-0.62 near target. Expect reach from low level in ~15-20s, then hold 0.55-0.65 without pumping hard. Safety caps force pump to 0 if filtered level exceeds 0.80 and limit to 0.25 above 0.70, so the 0.9 cutoff is never approached. Tolerates noisy readings and small dt jitter.", "predicted_behavior": "From low start (0.1-0.2): u~0.80 for ~12-15s, then taper to ~0.63 at 0.55 and ~0.58 at 0.6. Settling ~15-20s, inside 0.55-0.65 before 30s scoring window. Overshoot <0.02-0.03 (true level, filtered). Steady-state: mean error <0.015, time-in-band >90% after settling, steady duty ~0.57-0.62 (integral corrects feedforward bias). Energy ~0.33 per step steady (u^2). From near-target start: minimal transient.", "self_test_expectations": ["control({},first-call) returns finite u in [0,1] with yf init to y and i=0, no exception", "with constant y=0.2,target=0.6 repeated calls drive u to >=0.75 (fast fill) and stay <=0.85", "with constant y=0.6,target=0.6 output settles 0.40-0.70 and integral stays in [-0.20,0.25]", "with yf>0.82 output is 0.0 (high guard) and with yf>0.72 output <=0.25", "EMA filter with dt 0.1-0.4 on noisy y stays finite and state remains JSON-serializable with only yf,i keys"], "source_code": "import math
def _clamp(v, lo, hi):
    if not math.isfinite(v):
        return lo
    if v < lo:
        return lo
    if v > hi:
        return hi
    return v
def _ff_for_target(t):
    if not math.isfinite(t):
        t = 0.6
    if t < 0.0:
        t = 0.0
    if t > 1.0:
        t = 1.0
    ff = 0.57 + (t - 0.6) * 1.5
    if ff < 0.05:
        ff = 0.05
    if ff > 0.85:
        ff = 0.85
    return ff
def control(obs, state):
    try:
        y_raw = obs.get("y", 0.6)
        tgt_raw = obs.get("target", 0.6)
        dt_raw = obs.get("dt", 0.2)
    except Exception:
        return (0.0, {"yf": 0.6, "i": 0.0})
    try:
        y = float(y_raw)
    except Exception:
        y = 0.6
    try:
        target = float(tgt_raw)
    except Exception:
        target = 0.6
    try:
        dt = float(dt_raw)
    except Exception:
        dt = 0.2
    if not math.isfinite(y):
        y = target
    if not math.isfinite(target):
        target = 0.6
    if not math.isfinite(dt) or dt <= 0.0:
        dt = 0.2
    if dt < 0.02:
        dt = 0.02
    if dt > 1.0:
        dt = 1.0
    if y < -0.1:
        y = -0.1
    if y > 1.1:
        y = 1.1
    if target < 0.0:
        target = 0.0
    if target > 1.0:
        target = 1.0
    if not isinstance(state, dict):
        state = {}
    yf_prev = state.get("yf", None)
    i_prev = state.get("i", 0.0)
    try:
        yf_prev = float(yf_prev) if yf_prev is not None else y
    except Exception:
        yf_prev = y
    try:
        i_prev = float(i_prev)
    except Exception:
        i_prev = 0.0
    if not math.isfinite(yf_prev):
        yf_prev = y
    if not math.isfinite(i_prev):
        i_prev = 0.0
    if yf_prev < 0.0:
        yf_prev = 0.0
    if yf_prev > 1.0:
        yf_prev = 1.0
    if i_prev < -0.3:
        i_prev = -0.3
    if i_prev > 0.3:
        i_prev = 0.3
    tau_f = 0.8
    alpha = dt / (tau_f + dt)
    if alpha < 0.02:
        alpha = 0.02
    if alpha > 1.0:
        alpha = 1.0
    yf = alpha * y + (1.0 - alpha) * yf_prev
    yf = _clamp(yf, 0.0, 1.0)
    e = target - yf
    ff = _ff_for_target(target)
    Kp = 1.0
    Ki = 0.20
    p = Kp * e
    u_pre = ff + p + i_prev
    allow_int = True
    if abs(e) > 0.25:
        allow_int = False
    if u_pre >= 0.85 and e > 0.0:
        allow_int = False
    if u_pre <= 0.0 and e < 0.0:
        allow_int = False
    if allow_int:
        i_new = i_prev + Ki * e * dt
    else:
        i_new = i_prev * 0.999
    i_new = _clamp(i_new, -0.20, 0.25)
    u = ff + p + i_new
    if yf >= 0.80:
        u = 0.0
    elif yf > 0.70:
        if u > 0.25:
            u = 0.25
    u = _clamp(u, 0.0, 1.0)
    if not math.isfinite(u):
        u = 0.0
        i_new = 0.0
    return (float(u), {"yf": float(yf), "i": float(i_new)})
"}

{
  "change_summary": "Replaced aggressive PI (Kp=1.0,Ki=0.20,tau=0.8s,ff=0.57, hard cut only at 0.70/0.80) with delay-robust low-gain PI + asymmetric rate limiter + 6s look-ahead governor. Kp 1.0->0.40 with clipped error, Ki 0.20->0.05 with freeze when |e|>0.18 or yf>0.70, filter 0.8->1.5s, ff center 0.57->0.545, max increase 0.15/s / max decrease 0.60/s, safety caps 0.68->0.25 / 0.72->0.10 / 0.78->0 and predicted yf+6*slope caps 0.70->0.40 / 0.75->0.25. This caps in-flight pumping, stops windup during the 15s deadtime, and cuts early for water already in transit, while keeping same hold-u for nominal 1-2s plant.",
  "design_rationale": "Delay (not gain/outflow/sensor) explains traces, so loop bandwidth must be << 1/delay. Lower Kp/Ki and clipped P limit in-flight energy. Freezing integrator when far/high prevents delay windup. Slow-up/fast-down rate limit prevents bang-bang but allows safety cut. Filtered derivative with 6s prediction compensates transport lag: if yf+6*dslope>0.70 cut before overshoot arrives. Fixed ff ~0.545 preserves nominal hold 0.50-0.60 from E7-E10, so nominal 1-2s plant still reaches band. Safety ladder acts as reference governor for both plants.",
  "diagnosis": "Transport lag grew from ~1-2s to ~12-18s (~15s center) with similar steady gain. Evidence: after_change trace t132-187: u=0.75-0.95 from t140-155 holds y at 0.28-0.32 with no rise for ~15-19s, rise to 0.60 only at t165-171 (~0.02-0.03/s, same as E2/E5 nominal slope); after u cut to 0.25/0 at t174, y keeps rising 0.73->1.0 through t187 (>13s continued rise). Pre-change the same u=0.8 rose in 1-2s at 0.02-0.03/s. Post-change disturbance episodes show same: y rises while u is falling (e.g. Ep2 t80-100 y 0.61->0.63 while u 0.56->0.47) and falls long after cut, classic deadtime oscillation to 0.09-0.90 with 40 overrides/30 hard violations. No gain loss (eventual slope same), no faster drain (y stays at 1.0 for 10s at u=0), no sensor offset (lows ~0.06-0.10 and noise ~0.01 as in E1-E10).",
  "diagnosis_category": "response_slower",
  "machine_card": "Reservoir: u in [0,1] pump, y in [0,1] noisy level, target 0.6 band 0.55-0.65, soft 0.85 hard 0.90 forces 0. Nominal: positive nonlinear gain, hold-u ~0.54 for 0.6, drain to ~0 at u=0 tau ~8s, lag 1-2s, noise <0.01. Changed: pure delay ~15s added, gain/drain/noise unchanged. Controller must be low-bandwidth, anti-windup, predictive cut.",
  "operator_note": "Do not manually pump to 1.0 to chase low level; ~15s of pumped water is in transit. New controller intentionally caps at ~0.70-0.80 and approaches slowly. Expect 20-30s acquisition from low start, then tight hold near 0.545. If y>0.68 it will cut early even if still rising slowly - this is normal deadtime compensation. No action needed unless y>0.85.",
  "predicted_behavior": "Nominal (1-2s lag): from 0.17 rise at ~0.018/s with u~0.67 capped, enter 0.55-0.65 in ~20-25s, overshoot <0.70, MAE after 30s <0.02, in-band >0.90, no overrides. Delayed (~15s): same cap holds in-flight energy <0.375 rise in transit, prediction cuts at yf~0.65-0.68 to 0.25/0.10, overshoot peaks <0.80-0.85, no hard >0.90 violations, slow oscillation damped to band within ~60-80s, in-band after settling >0.70, MAE ~0.03-0.06 vs 0.21 before.",
  "self_test_expectations": [
    "cold start y=0.2 target 0.6 -> first u 0.60-0.72, not 0.95-1.0, finite",
    "hold y=0.60 target 0.6 -> u stays 0.50-0.60, drift <0.05 in 10 steps",
    "high y=0.75 target 0.6 -> u capped <=0.10 within 1 step, yf>=0.78 -> u=0",
    "rising fast yf=0.64 slope 0.02 -> predicted 0.76 -> u capped <=0.25 even though yf<0.68",
